        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: قحط",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قحط — qahat — \"a famine\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اس سال گاؤں میں قحط پڑا۔ is sāl gāoṅ meṅ qahat paṛā. This year there was a famine in the village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قحط (qahat) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic qaḥṭ, \"drought, a failure of rain\". A famine is said to fall: قحط پڑا."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
